            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0667" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/2889: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-26T16:00:00-04:00">June 26, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>291. Department’s 202, June 20, 7 p.m. Cabinet agreed to Department’s suggested
                    clauses regarding air field contract June 24 and Council of State of June 25.
                    Final draft is scheduled to be approved by Council June 30 and signed by
                    President. I still have my fingers crossed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
